---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Equera"
  description="Equera Privacy Policy - Learn how we protect your personal information."
>
  <article class="py-20 lg:py-32 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">Effective Date: November 12th, 2026</p>

        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
          <p>
            Danielle Finch, doing business as “Equera” (“we,” “our,” “us”) respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and share your information when you use our platform and services.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">1. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>We may collect the following types of personal information:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Sign-Up Information (B2B):</strong> name, email address, phone number, company name, and company address.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Booking Requests (B2C):</strong> name, email address, phone number, number of travelers, travel dates, and special requests.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Device Information:</strong> if you upload photos from your device into our product catalog, we may request access to your device’s storage for that purpose only.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Cookies and Similar Technologies:</strong> we collect information through cookies and similar tools. These may include session cookies, analytics cookies, and other technologies used by our website host (Framer).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>AI Assistants:</strong> the search and booking details described in “Using Equera through an AI assistant” below.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-6 mb-2">Using Equera through an AI assistant</h3>
          <p>
            Equera offers a connector that lets AI assistants, such as Claude or ChatGPT, search our public catalogue of stays, experiences and trips, check dates and prices, and, where we have switched it on, start a booking. You add the connector in your assistant. It needs no Equera account.
          </p>
          <p><strong>What we collect (data categories).</strong></p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Searches and date checks:</strong> each request an assistant makes leaves a record: the tool used, the name the assistant gives for itself (for example “claude”), whether it worked and how long it took, the search filters (country, type of listing, category, kind of stay, dates, number of guests, price limit and currency, sort order), how many results came back, and which listings were checked. It also keeps the words of the search (what was searched for and where), after we take out email addresses, phone numbers and web addresses; even so, please do not put personal details in a search. No name, email address, phone number, booking reference, IP address, account or conversation is stored with these records.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Booking in the chat</strong> (where we have switched it on): your name, email address and phone number, and, if you choose, your country and a note for the host. We also keep the language of the booking form, so that emails about the booking are in that language. The assistant may fill these in from your conversation. You check them, and nothing is sent until you press the button. Payment never happens in the chat: any deposit is paid on Equera’s own booking page.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Booking links by email:</strong> the email address you give when you ask the assistant to send your booking links. We send one email to it, with a link to each booking made with that address in the last 12 months, and nothing if it has no bookings.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not receive your conversation with the assistant. ChatGPT also sends an anonymous identifier for the conversation; we use it only to keep the results shown in one conversation in order, and we do not store it. The company that provides your assistant handles the conversation under its own privacy policy.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Why we use it (purposes).</strong> Search records: to answer the assistant, to understand what travellers look for and which places and activities are missing, and to keep the service working. Booking details: to make and manage that booking, and to email you and tell the host about it; for a booking made on Equera’s site, this includes a reminder if a booking with a deposit is left unpaid. We do not use them for other marketing. When you book from a link or the form, we also record which assistant the booking came from.</p>
          <p><strong>Who receives it (recipient categories).</strong> The host of the listing you book receives your booking details. Our service providers for hosting, email and messaging receive what they need to run the service (see “How We Share Your Information”). Booking emails are sent through our email provider. Our customer messaging provider, currently Braze, receives the following. For a booking made in the chat: nothing until its deposit is paid or the host confirms it; from then on, a record of each later step (paid, cancelled, completed) with the booking number, the listing and its type, how it was booked, the number of guests and the start date (and, when it is paid, the total and currency), filed under a one-way code made from your email address, not the address itself. For a booking made on Equera’s site, including from an assistant’s link: when it is made, your email address, your first name and, if you gave it, your country, with the same booking details plus the total, the currency, whether a deposit is due and the listing’s country; then a record of each later step (paid, expired, cancelled, completed). The reminder for an unpaid deposit booking is sent through Braze. On Equera’s booking page, and only if you accept marketing cookies, Braze’s web tool may ask to send you notifications, and records that you submitted a payment with its currency and amount, without your email address or the booking. If we switch on meaning-based search, the cleaned search words (email addresses, phone numbers and links removed), and nothing else, are sent to our embeddings provider (currently OpenAI) to find listings close in meaning.</p>
          <p><strong>How long we keep it (retention).</strong> Search words (what was searched for and where): 90 days, then removed from the record. The rest of each search record (the tool, the assistant's name, the filters, the result counts and the listings checked): 13 months, then deleted. A booking made through an assistant is kept like any other Equera booking. Booking details: as long as we keep any booking (see “Data Retention”). The email address for booking links is used to send that one email; a record of the sent email is kept as for our other emails.</p>
          <p><strong>Your choices (user controls).</strong> You can remove the Equera connector from your assistant at any time. You decide what goes into a search and into the booking form, and you can change any detail before you send it. To see, correct or delete the details of a booking, contact us using the details in “Contact Us” below. Because search records hold no name or contact details, we cannot find which of them came from you.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Provide and manage our services, including booking requests and product catalog features.</li>
            <li>Communicate with you, including via WhatsApp Business and email, on behalf of travel organizations.</li>
            <li>Respond to your inquiries and provide customer support.</li>
            <li>Improve our platform, services, and user experience.</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">3. How We Share Your Information</h2>
          <p>We may share your information with:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Travel Organizations:</strong> to process booking requests and related communications.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Service Providers:</strong> such as hosting providers, communication tools (e.g., WhatsApp, email services), and analytics providers.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Legal Authorities:</strong> if required to comply with legal obligations, enforce our terms, or protect rights, safety, or property.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties.</p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">4. International Data Transfers</h2>
          <p>
            Because we operate internationally, your personal information may be transferred to and processed in countries outside of your own. Where required by law (e.g., GDPR in the European Union), we will ensure that adequate safeguards are in place to protect your data.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">5. Data Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We retain your personal information only as long as necessary to provide our services, fulfill booking requests, comply with legal obligations, and resolve disputes. When data is no longer needed, we will securely delete or anonymize it in accordance with common industry practices.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">6. Your Rights</h2>
          <p>Depending on your location, you may have rights under applicable data protection laws, such as:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>The right to access the information we hold about you.</li>
            <li>The right to request correction, deletion, or restriction of your data.</li>
            <li>The right to object to certain uses of your data.</li>
            <li>The right to data portability.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If you wish to exercise these rights, please contact us using the details below.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">7. Security</h2>
          <p>
            We take reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your personal information against loss, misuse, and unauthorized access. However, no method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">8. Children’s Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our services are not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If we learn that a child under 16 has provided personal information, we will delete it promptly.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you by posting the updated policy on our website and revising the “Effective Date” above.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">10. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, you can contact us at:</p>
          <p>
            Danielle Finch<br />
            Email: <a href="mailto:danielle@equera.ai">danielle@equera.ai</a><br />
            Address: Almstadrstraße 42, 10119, Berlin
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark-purple mt-8 mb-2">11. Cookie Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We use cookies and similar technologies to enhance your experience on our platform. Cookies are small text files stored on your device that help us recognize you and remember your preferences.
          </p>
          <p>Types of cookies we may use:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> necessary for the website to function.</li>
            <li><strong>Analytics Cookies:</strong> to understand how users interact with our platform (e.g., through tools provided by our hosting provider, Framer).</li>
            <li><strong>Functional Cookies:</strong> to remember your preferences and improve your experience.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings. Please note that disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality of our services.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
